{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Independent merged-tree documentation review PASS. Reviewer session codex:/root/closeout_keen_7ec29192 did not author the remediation. I reviewed merged commit 7ec291928fa1febddccfd97c17668c0b4488fd5c against immutable audit base 0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e and confirmed it is blob-identical on all three target paths to reviewed candidate d7a16a3d25ada01893510dd622ed1c208b6295be. All non-comment, nonblank TOML lines are byte-identical; path-scoped diff --check passes. I independently checked every edited prose block against the current config resolver and workflow consumers. The six rows collectively cover every Scope constraint and every named consumer contract. No findings. TSV columns: path/block, pinned-before citation, final citation, preserved scope/consumer contract, contract check, before words, after words, semantic-preservation, bloat-removal, reviewer session.\n.github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml#L1-L9\t0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e:.github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml:L1-L9\t7ec291928fa1febddccfd97c17668c0b4488fd5c:.github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml:L1-L3\tThe direct-Anthropic arm remains selected through REBAR_LLM_CONFIG_FILE even though it matches defaults, and names ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; this preserves overlay-path coverage for external-integration, structured-output-baseline, and Jira rich-text consumers.\tPASS\t81\t25\tPASS\tPASS\tcodex:/root/closeout_keen_7ec29192\n.github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml#L11-L20\t0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e:.github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml:L11-L20\t7ec291928fa1febddccfd97c17668c0b4488fd5c:.github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml:L5-L7\tThe provider-qualified scalar model and all three class slots remain explicit, preserving cfg.model and class-resolver behavior and preventing ambient Anthropic selection from leaking into another provider arm.\tPASS\t112\t38\tPASS\tPASS\tcodex:/root/closeout_keen_7ec29192\n.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml#L1-L19\t0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e:.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml:L1-L19\t7ec291928fa1febddccfd97c17668c0b4488fd5c:.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml:L1-L8\tThe Bedrock arm still uses the Anthropic arm's Claude families for provider-only comparison, requires inference-profile IDs with nonuniform suffixes copied from AWS discovery, uses ambient AWS credentials, and tells workflow consumers to set both AWS_DEFAULT_REGION and REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION.\tPASS\t164\t76\tPASS\tPASS\tcodex:/root/closeout_keen_7ec29192\n.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml#L21-L38\t0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e:.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml:L21-L38\t7ec291928fa1febddccfd97c17668c0b4488fd5c:.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml:L10-L13\tThe provider-qualified scalar model and every class slot remain explicit; provider-matrix consumers still blank ANTHROPIC_API_KEY to prevent masquerading, while the text keeps that isolation scoped to the matrix and preserves the approved direct-Anthropic fallback elsewhere.\tPASS\t206\t47\tPASS\tPASS\tcodex:/root/closeout_keen_7ec29192\n.github/llm-providers/openai.toml#L1-L12\t0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e:.github/llm-providers/openai.toml:L1-L12\t7ec291928fa1febddccfd97c17668c0b4488fd5c:.github/llm-providers/openai.toml:L1-L3\tThe overlay still identifies OpenAI as the best-effort provider tier, names OPENAI_API_KEY, and records that all three configured model IDs were verified against the repository account on 2026-08-03.\tPASS\t84\t26\tPASS\tPASS\tcodex:/root/closeout_keen_7ec29192\n.github/llm-providers/openai.toml#L14-L23\t0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e:.github/llm-providers/openai.toml:L14-L23\t7ec291928fa1febddccfd97c17668c0b4488fd5c:.github/llm-providers/openai.toml:L5-L7\tThe provider-qualified scalar model and every class slot remain explicit for config and class resolvers, preserving OpenAI selection and preventing the bare cfg.model default from defeating workflow provider isolation.\tPASS\t112\t29\tPASS\tPASS\tcodex:/root/closeout_keen_7ec29192"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789059034943104001,"uuid":"4f704f64-dfa9-4b82-979c-b58b04e025ed"}